        if h[p] >= h[i]:
```
hint: The parent of index i is at (i − 1) // 2.
hint: Stop as soon as the parent is no bigger than the item.
right: Each new item climbs while its parent is bigger and stops under a parent that's no bigger: `[1, 3, 2, 5, 4, 8]`.
wrong: `sift_up` loops while i > 0: find the parent p = (i − 1) // 2, break if `h[p] <= h[i]`, otherwise swap and set `i = p`. `push` appends, then sifts up from the last index.

