=== task: multi medium
title: What things cost
prompt: Choose **every** cost that is correct for a heap of n items.
* Heapify a list of n items: O(n) :: Right. Less than n swaps in total.
* The k smallest of n items, by heapify and k pops: O(n + k log n) :: Right. O(n) to heapify, then O(log n) per pop.
* Merging k sorted lists with N items in total: O(N log k) :: Right. Each item is pushed and popped once, in a heap of at most k items.
* Heap sort of n items: O(n log n) :: Right. n pops, each O(log n).
- n pushes, one at a time: O(n) :: Each push can take O(log n) swaps: O(n log n) in total. That's why heapify exists.
- Peeking at the smallest item: O(log n) :: It's always at index 0: O(1).
hint: Which jobs walk one path per item, and which do almost nothing per item?
hint: Peeking doesn't change the heap at all.
right: Heapify O(n), k smallest O(n + k log n), merging O(N log k) and heap sort O(n log n). Pushing items one at a time costs O(n log n), and a peek is O(1).
wrong: Each push or pop costs O(log n), so n pushes cost O(n log n). Heapify is O(n), and peeking at `h[0]` is O(1).

